{"id":"mahabharata-9-026","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":26,"title":"षड्विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 26 · Duryodhana's brother Sudarshana killed","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana and Sudarshana, the survivors, are attacked by Bhima, who cuts off Sudarshana's head with a razor-headed arrow. Duryodhana's heart is crushed, and the two armies fall upon each other in the evening light.","kn":"ಉಳಿದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ-ಸುದರ್ಶನರ ಮೇಲೆ ಭೀಮ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡಿ ಕ್ಷುರಬಾಣದಿಂದ ಸುದರ್ಶನನ ತಲೆ ಕತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಹೃದಯ ಜರ್ಜರಿತವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ಸಂಜೆ ಬೆಳಕಿನಲ್ಲಿ ಎರಡೂ ಸೈನ್ಯಗಳು ಒಂದರ ಮೇಲೊಂದು ಬೀಳುತ್ತವೆ.","hi":"बचे दुर्योधन और सुदर्शन पर भीम आक्रमण करते हैं और क्षुर बाण से सुदर्शन का सिर काट देते हैं। दुर्योधन का हृदय टूट जाता है और सन्ध्या के प्रकाश में दोनों सेनाएँ एक-दूसरे पर टूट पड़ती हैं।","te":"మిగిలిన దుర్యోధనుడు, సుదర్శనునిపై భీముడు దాడి చేసి క్షురబాణంతో సుదర్శనుని తల నరుకుతాడు. దుర్యోధనుని హృదయం ముక్కలవుతుంది; సాయంకాల వెలుగులో ఇరు సేనలు ఒకదానిపై ఒకటి పడతాయి.","ta":"எஞ்சிய துரியோதனன், சுதர்சனன் மீது பீமன் தாக்கி க்ஷுர அம்பால் சுதர்சனனின் தலையை வெட்டுகிறான். துரியோதனனின் இதயம் நொறுங்க, மாலை ஒளியில் இரு படைகளும் ஒன்றன் மேல் ஒன்று விழுகின்றன.","ml":"ശേഷിച്ചവരായ ദുര്യോധനനെയും സുദർശനനെയും ഭീമൻ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ക്ഷുരപ്രം പോലെയുള്ള അമ്പുകൊണ്ട് സുദർശനന്റെ തല അറുക്കുന്നു. ദുര്യോധനന്റെ ഹൃദയം തകരുന്നു; സന്ധ്യാവെളിച്ചത്തിൽ ഇരുസേനകളും പരസ്പരം ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.26; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दुर्योधनो महाराज सुदर्शश्चापि ते सुतः ।\nहतशेषौ तदा संख्ये वाजिमध्ये व्यवस्थितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, O great king, and your son Sudarsha, the only ones left, then stood in the battle in the midst of horses."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनं दृष्ट्वा वाजिमध्ये व्यवस्थितम् ।\nउवाच देवकीपुत्रः कुन्तीपुत्रं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing Duryodhana standing among the horses, Devaki's son said to Kunti's son Dhananjaya:"}},{"n":3,"text":"शत्रवो हतभूयिष्ठा ज्ञातयः परिपालिताः ।\nगृहीत्वा संजयं चासौ निवृत्तः शिनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The enemies are mostly slain and your kinsmen are protected. That bull of the Shini line, Satyaki, has turned back after taking Sanjaya."}},{"n":4,"text":"परिश्रान्तश्च नकुलः सहदेवश्च भारत ।\nयोधयित्वा रणे पापान्धार्तराष्ट्रपदानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula and Sahadeva, O Bharata, are weary from fighting in the battle the wicked followers of the Dhartarashtra."}},{"n":5,"text":"सुयोधनमभित्यज्य त्रय एते व्यवस्थिताः ।\nकृपश्च कृतवर्मा च द्रौणिश्चैव महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only these three stand by Suyodhana, leaving the rest: Kripa, Kritavarman and the great chariot-fighter Drona's son."}},{"n":6,"text":"असौ तिष्ठति पाञ्चाल्यः श्रिया परमया युतः ।\nदुर्योधनबलं हत्वा सह सर्वैः प्रभद्रकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchala stands there in great splendor, having killed Duryodhana's force with all the Prabhadrakas."}},{"n":7,"text":"असौ दुर्योधनः पार्थ वाजिमध्ये व्यवस्थितः ।\nछत्रेण ध्रियमाणेन प्रेक्षमाणो मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is Duryodhana, Partha, standing among the horses, with the parasol held over him, looking about again and again."}},{"n":8,"text":"प्रतिव्यूह्य बलं सर्वं रणमध्ये व्यवस्थितः ।\nएनं हत्वा शितैर्बाणैः कृतकृत्यो भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"He has drawn up all his force in counter-array and stands in the middle of the battle. Kill him with sharp arrows and you will have done what was to be done."}},{"n":9,"text":"गजानीकं हतं दृष्ट्वा त्वां च प्राप्तमरिंदम ।\nयावन्न विद्रवन्त्येते तावज्जहि सुयोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the elephant force killed and you arrived, tamer of foes, kill Suyodhana before these men flee."}},{"n":10,"text":"यातु कश्चित्तु पाञ्चाल्यं क्षिप्रमागम्यतामिति ।\nपरिश्रान्तबलस्तात नैष मुच्येत किल्बिषी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let someone go and quickly call the Panchala here. Dear friend, with his force worn out, this sinner must not escape."}},{"n":11,"text":"तव हत्वा बलं सर्वं संग्रामे धृतराष्ट्रजः ।\nजितान्पाण्डुसुतान्मत्वा रूपं धारयते महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having destroyed all your force in the battle, the son of Dhritarashtra takes on a grand appearance, thinking the sons of Pandu beaten."}},{"n":12,"text":"निहतं स्वबलं दृष्ट्वा पीडितं चापि पाण्डवैः ।\nध्रुवमेष्यति संग्रामे वधायैवात्मनो नृपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his own force killed and tormented by the Pandavas, the king will surely come into the battle just to get himself killed.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"एवमुक्तः फल्गुनस्तु कृष्णं वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nधृतराष्ट्रसुताः सर्वे हता भीमेन मानद ।\nयावेतावास्थितौ कृष्ण तावद्य न भविष्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Phalguna spoke these words to Krishna: \"All the sons of Dhritarashtra have been killed by Bhima, O giver of honor; those two who stand here, Krishna, will not be alive today."}},{"n":14,"text":"हतो भीष्मो हतो द्रोणः कर्णो वैकर्तनो हतः ।\nमद्रराजो हतः शल्यो हतः कृष्ण जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma is slain, Drona is slain, Karna Vaikartana is slain, the Madra king Shalya is slain, and Jayadratha, Krishna, is slain."}},{"n":15,"text":"हयाः पञ्चशताः शिष्टाः शकुनेः सौबलस्य च ।\nरथानां तु शते शिष्टे द्वे एव तु जनार्दन ।\nदन्तिनां च शतं साग्रं त्रिसाहस्राः पदातयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of Shakuni son of Subala five hundred horses remain; of chariots, Janardana, only two hundred remain; of elephants a hundred and a little more, and three thousand foot soldiers."}},{"n":16,"text":"अश्वत्थामा कृपश्चैव त्रिगर्ताधिपतिस्तथा ।\nउलूकः शकुनिश्चैव कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ashvatthama, Kripa, the lord of the Trigartas, Uluka, Shakuni and the Satvata Kritavarman:"}},{"n":17,"text":"एतद्बलमभूच्छेषं धार्तराष्ट्रस्य माधव ।\nमोक्षो न नूनं कालाद्धि विद्यते भुवि कस्यचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"this is the force that remains to the Dhartarashtra, Madhava. Surely no one on earth has any release from Time."}},{"n":18,"text":"तथा विनिहते सैन्ये पश्य दुर्योधनं स्थितम् ।\nअद्याह्ना हि महाराजो हतामित्रो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the army destroyed like this, look at Duryodhana standing there. Today the great king will have his foes slain."}},{"n":19,"text":"न हि मे मोक्ष्यते कश्चित्परेषामिति चिन्तये ।\nये त्वद्य समरं कृष्ण न हास्यन्ति रणोत्कटाः ।\nतान्वै सर्वान्हनिष्यामि यद्यपि स्युरमानुषाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think none of the enemy will escape me. Those fierce fighters who do not abandon the battle today, Krishna, I will kill every one of them, even if they were not human."}},{"n":20,"text":"अद्य युद्धे सुसंक्रुद्धो दीर्घं राज्ञः प्रजागरम् ।\nअपनेष्यामि गान्धारं पातयित्वा शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, in a great rage, I will end the king's long wakefulness, the Gandhara prince, by felling him with sharp arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"निकृत्या वै दुराचारो यानि रत्नानि सौबलः ।\nसभायामहरद्द्यूते पुनस्तान्याहराम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The jewels that the wicked son of Subala took by trickery in the dice game in the assembly, I will take back again."}},{"n":22,"text":"अद्य ता अपि वेत्स्यन्ति सर्वा नागपुरस्त्रियः ।\nश्रुत्वा पतींश्च पुत्रांश्च पाण्डवैर्निहतान्युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today all the women of Nagapura too will learn, hearing that their husbands and sons have been killed in battle by the Pandavas."}},{"n":23,"text":"समाप्तमद्य वै कर्म सर्वं कृष्ण भविष्यति ।\nअद्य दुर्योधनो दीप्तां श्रियं प्राणांश्च त्यक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today, Krishna, the whole task will be completed. Today Duryodhana will give up his blazing fortune and his life."}},{"n":24,"text":"नापयाति भयात्कृष्ण संग्रामाद्यदि चेन्मम ।\nनिहतं विद्धि वार्ष्णेय धार्तराष्ट्रं सुबालिशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the Dhartarashtra does not run from the battle in fear, Vrishni, know that the childish man is slain."}},{"n":25,"text":"मम ह्येतदशक्तं वै वाजिवृन्दमरिंदम ।\nसोढुं ज्यातलनिर्घोषं याहि यावन्निहन्म्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This herd of horses cannot bear the twang of the bowstring, tamer of foes; go on, while I strike.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु दाशार्हः पाण्डवेन यशस्विना ।\nअचोदयद्धयान्राजन्दुर्योधनबलं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the renowned Pandava, the Dasharha urged the horses toward Duryodhana's force, O king."}},{"n":27,"text":"तदनीकमभिप्रेक्ष्य त्रयः सज्जा महारथाः ।\nभीमसेनोऽर्जुनश्चैव सहदेवश्च मारिष ।\nप्रययुः सिंहनादेन दुर्योधनजिघांसया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that force, three ready great chariot-fighters, Bhimasena, Arjuna and Sahadeva, O revered one, advanced with a lion's roar, wishing to kill Duryodhana."}},{"n":28,"text":"तान्प्रेक्ष्य सहितान्सर्वाञ्जवेनोद्यतकार्मुकान् ।\nसौबलोऽभ्यद्रवद्युद्धे पाण्डवानाततायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them all together, bows raised in haste, Shakuni, son of Subala, rushed in the battle at the murderous Pandavas."}},{"n":29,"text":"सुदर्शनस्तव सुतो भीमसेनं समभ्ययात् ।\nसुशर्मा शकुनिश्चैव युयुधाते किरीटिना ।\nसहदेवं तव सुतो हयपृष्ठगतोऽभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son Sudarshana attacked Bhimasena; Susharma and Shakuni fought the diadem-wearer; and your son, mounted on a horse, attacked Sahadeva."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो ह्ययत्नतः क्षिप्रं तव पुत्रो जनाधिप ।\nप्रासेन सहदेवस्य शिरसि प्राहरद्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O lord of men, your son quickly and without effort struck Sahadeva hard on the head with a spear."}},{"n":31,"text":"सोपाविशद्रथोपस्थे तव पुत्रेण ताडितः ।\nरुधिराप्लुतसर्वाङ्ग आशीविष इव श्वसन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by your son, Sahadeva sank down on the seat of his chariot, his whole body drenched in blood, hissing like a venomous snake."}},{"n":32,"text":"प्रतिलभ्य ततः संज्ञां सहदेवो विशां पते ।\nदुर्योधनं शरैस्तीक्ष्णैः संक्रुद्धः समवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regaining consciousness, O lord of the people, Sahadeva, furious, covered Duryodhana with sharp arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"पार्थोऽपि युधि विक्रम्य कुन्तीपुत्रो धनंजयः ।\nशूराणामश्वपृष्ठेभ्यः शिरांसि निचकर्त ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha too, Kunti's son Dhananjaya, showing his prowess in the battle, cut off the heads of heroes from their horses."}},{"n":34,"text":"तदनीकं तदा पार्थो व्यधमद्बहुभिः शरैः ।\nपातयित्वा हयान्सर्वांस्त्रिगर्तानां रथान्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha shattered that force with many arrows, brought down all the horses and advanced on the chariots of the Trigartas."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्ते सहिता भूत्वा त्रिगर्तानां महारथाः ।\nअर्जुनं वासुदेवं च शरवर्षैरवाकिरन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those great chariot-fighters of the Trigartas, uniting, covered Arjuna and Vasudeva with showers of arrows."}},{"n":36,"text":"सत्यकर्माणमाक्षिप्य क्षुरप्रेण महायशाः ।\nततोऽस्य स्यन्दनस्येषां चिच्छिदे पाण्डुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having struck Satyakarman with a razor-headed arrow, the renowned son of Pandu cut the shaft of his chariot."}},{"n":37,"text":"शिलाशितेन च विभो क्षुरप्रेण महायशाः ।\nशिरश्चिच्छेद प्रहसंस्तप्तकुण्डलभूषणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O lord, with a razor-headed arrow whetted on stone, the renowned man, laughing, cut off his head, adorned with burnished earrings."}},{"n":38,"text":"सत्येषुमथ चादत्त योधानां मिषतां ततः ।\nयथा सिंहो वने राजन्मृगं परिबुभुक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, while the warriors looked on, he took Satyeshu too, as a hungry lion in a forest takes a deer, O king."}},{"n":39,"text":"तं निहत्य ततः पार्थः सुशर्माणं त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nविद्ध्वा तानहनत्सर्वान्रथान्रुक्मविभूषितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed him, Partha pierced Susharma with three arrows and killed all those gold-adorned chariot-fighters."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततस्तु प्रत्वरन्पार्थो दीर्घकालं सुसंभृतम् ।\nमुञ्चन्क्रोधविषं तीक्ष्णं प्रस्थलाधिपतिं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Partha, pressing on, loosed against the lord of Prasthala the sharp poison of his anger, long and well stored up."}},{"n":41,"text":"तमर्जुनः पृषत्कानां शतेन भरतर्षभ ।\nपूरयित्वा ततो वाहान्न्यहनत्तस्य धन्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, O bull of the Bharatas, filled that archer's horses with a hundred arrows and killed them."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततः शरं समादाय यमदण्डोपमं शितम् ।\nसुशर्माणं समुद्दिश्य चिक्षेपाशु हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he took a sharp arrow like the staff of Yama and, aiming at Susharma, shot it quickly, as if laughing."}},{"n":43,"text":"स शरः प्रेषितस्तेन क्रोधदीप्तेन धन्विना ।\nसुशर्माणं समासाद्य बिभेद हृदयं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"That arrow, sent by the archer blazing with anger, reached Susharma and split his heart in the battle."}},{"n":44,"text":"स गतासुर्महाराज पपात धरणीतले ।\nनन्दयन्पाण्डवान्सर्वान्व्यथयंश्चापि तावकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lifeless, O great king, he fell to the ground, gladdening all the Pandavas and distressing your men."}},{"n":45,"text":"सुशर्माणं रणे हत्वा पुत्रानस्य महारथान् ।\nसप्त चाष्टौ च त्रिंशच्च सायकैरनयत्क्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed Susharma in the battle, Arjuna sent his great chariot-fighter sons, seven, eight and thirty, to destruction with arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततोऽस्य निशितैर्बाणैः सर्वान्हत्वा पदानुगान् ।\nअभ्यगाद्भारतीं सेनां हतशेषां महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then with sharp arrows he killed all his foot followers, and the great chariot-fighter approached the remnant of the Kuru army."}},{"n":47,"text":"भीमस्तु समरे क्रुद्धः पुत्रं तव जनाधिप ।\nसुदर्शनमदृश्यं तं शरैश्चक्रे हसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Bhima, enraged in the battle, as if laughing, made your son Sudarshana invisible with arrows."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततोऽस्य प्रहसन्क्रुद्धः शिरः कायादपाहरत् ।\nक्षुरप्रेण सुतीक्ष्णेन स हतः प्रापतद्भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, laughing in anger, he cut Sudarshana's head from his body with a very sharp razor-headed arrow, and he fell dead to the ground."}},{"n":49,"text":"तस्मिंस्तु निहते वीरे ततस्तस्य पदानुगाः ।\nपरिवव्रू रणे भीमं किरन्तो विशिखाञ्शितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that hero was killed, his followers surrounded Bhima in the battle, scattering sharp arrows."}},{"n":50,"text":"ततस्तु निशितैर्बाणैस्तदनीकं वृकोदरः ।\nइन्द्राशनिसमस्पर्शैः समन्तात्पर्यवाकिरत् ।\nततः क्षणेन तद्भीमो न्यहनद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vrikodara covered that force on every side with sharp arrows that touched like Indra's thunderbolt, and in a moment, O bull of the Bharatas, Bhima destroyed it."}},{"n":51,"text":"तेषु तूत्साद्यमानेषु सेनाध्यक्षा महाबलाः ।\nभीमसेनं समासाद्य ततोऽयुध्यन्त भारत ।\nतांस्तु सर्वाञ्शरैर्घोरैरवाकिरत पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they were being cut down, the mighty commanders of the army reached Bhimasena and fought him, O Bharata; but the Pandava covered them all with dreadful arrows."}},{"n":52,"text":"तथैव तावका राजन्पाण्डवेयान्महारथान् ।\nशरवर्षेण महता समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way your men, O king, surrounded the great chariot-fighters of the Pandavas on every side with a great shower of arrows."}},{"n":53,"text":"व्याकुलं तदभूत्सर्वं पाण्डवानां परैः सह ।\nतावकानां च समरे पाण्डवेयैर्युयुत्सताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everything became confused, the Pandavas with their foes and your men fighting the Pandavas in the battle."}},{"n":54,"text":"तत्र योधास्तदा पेतुः परस्परसमाहताः ।\nउभयोः सेनयो राजन्संशोचन्तः स्म बान्धवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There the warriors fell, struck by one another, and the armies on both sides, O king, mourned their kinsmen."}}]}]}